<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orval Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1070</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orval Abbey is a Cistercian monastery in the Gaume region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, near the French border. Founded in 1070 by Benedictine monks from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a> with the support of the counts of Chiny, it joined the Cistercian order in 1132 and became wealthy and influential. Destroyed by French revolutionary troops in 1793, it was rebuilt in the 20th century and is known for its Trappist beer.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orval-abbey.jpg" alt="Orval Abbey" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Etychon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orval_church_etychon_200611.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
